## Install
{% if repository %}
```bash
# as a CLI
uv tool install git+{{ repository }}

# as a library, from another project
uv add "{{ name }} @ git+{{ repository }}"

# once, without installing
uvx --from git+{{ repository }} {{ name }} --help
```
{% else %}
From a clone of the repository:

```bash
# as a CLI
uv tool install .

# as a library, from another project
uv add /path/to/{{ name }}
```
{% endif %}
## Use it

Run `{{ name }} --help`. It prints the tool's skill: when to use it, every capability,
worked invocations, sharp edges, and which files to read. Follow it. Confirm every argument
against `{{ name }} <command> --help` rather than memory.
